content.content:
===== GET /v1/baselines
Returns list of the mSCP baselines allowed for the Compliance benchmarks

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BaselinesResponse"}}}, "description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 401 {"description": "Unauthorized request"}
  resp 403 {"description": "Insufficient permissions"}
===== GET /v1/benchmarks
Returns list of tenant benchmarks (if any)

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarksResponseV2"}}}, "description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 401 {"description": "Unauthorized request"}
  resp 403 {"description": "Insufficient permissions"}
===== POST /v1/benchmarks
Creates a new benchmark from provided benchmark request and deploys associated artifacts to the MDM

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:create`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  resp 202 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarkResponseV2"}}}, "description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 400 {"description": "Invalid benchmark request"}
  resp 401 {"description": "Unauthorized request"}
  resp 403 {"description": "Insufficient permissions"}
  resp 409 {"description": "Benchmark with the same title exists already or database write conflict occurred"}
  body {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarkRequestV2"}}}, "required": true}
===== DELETE /v1/benchmarks/{id}
Removes benchmark with given benchmark and removes associated draft (if any) and artifacts from the MDM

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:delete`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Given benchmark ID", "in": "path", "name": "id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  resp 204 {"description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 400 {"description": "Invalid benchmark request or missing benchmark ID"}
  resp 401 {"description": "Unauthorized request"}
  resp 403 {"description": "Insufficient permissions"}
===== GET /v1/benchmarks/{id}
Returns benchmark with full configuration for given benchmark ID, or 404 if not found

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Given benchmark ID", "in": "path", "name": "id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarkResponseV2"}}}, "description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 400 {"description": "Missing benchmark ID"}
  resp 401 {"description": "Unauthorized request"}
  resp 403 {"description": "Insufficient permissions"}
  resp 404 {"description": "Benchmark not found"}
===== GET /v1/benchmarks/{id}/compliance-percentage
Calculates and returns the overall compliance percentage for a specific benchmark report as sum of device compliance scores divided by number of devices

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Tenant's benchmark ID", "in": "path", "name": "id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/CompliancePercentage"}}}, "description": "Successful response with compliance percentage"}
  resp 400 {"$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"}
  resp 404 {"description": "Benchmark has no applicable rules for reporting calculations"}
===== GET /v1/benchmarks/{id}/devices
Provides devices filtered report for a specific benchmark rule

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Tenant's benchmark ID", "in": "path", "name": "id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  param {"in": "query", "name": "rule-id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  param {"description": "Search devices with matching device name or device ID", "in": "query", "name": "device-search", "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  param {"in": "query", "name": "rule-result", "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/RuleResultState"}}
  param {"description": "Page number (0-based index, default is 0)", "in": "query", "name": "page", "schema": {"default": 0, "minimum": 0, "type": "integer"}}
  param {"description": "Number of results per page (default is 100)", "in": "query", "name": "page-size", "schema": {"default": 100, "minimum": 1, "type": "integer"}}
  param {"description": "Sort order of result (e.g., 'deviceName:asc', 'ruleResult:desc'). Supports chained sorting like 'deviceName,ruleResult:desc'. Ascending order is default and in such a case doesn't require to be specified.", "in": "query", "name": "sort", "schema": {"default": "ruleResult:desc", "type": "string"}}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarkRuleDevicesResponse"}}}, "description": "Successful response"}
  resp 400 {"$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"}
===== GET /v1/benchmarks/{id}/rules
Provides benchmark rules stats for a specific benchmark

**Required Permissions:** `compliance-benchmarks:read`
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Tenant's benchmark ID", "in": "path", "name": "id", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  param {"description": "string to search in rule title and rule id", "in": "query", "name": "rule-search", "schema": {"type": "string"}}
  param {"description": "Page number (0-based index, default is 0)", "in": "query", "name": "page", "schema": {"default": 0, "minimum": 0, "type": "integer"}}
  param {"description": "Number of results per page (default is 500)", "in": "query", "name": "page-size", "schema": {"default": 500, "minimum": 1, "type": "integer"}}
  param {"description": "Sort order of result (e.g., 'ruleTitle:asc', 'passed:desc', 'failed:desc', 'unknown:desc'). Supports chained sorting like 'ruleId,passed:desc'. Ascending order is default and in such a case doesn't require to be specified, such as 'ruleNumber,ruleTitle'.", "in": "query", "name": "sort", "schema": {"default": "ruleNumber,ruleTitle", "type": "string"}}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/BenchmarkRulesStatsResponse"}}}, "description": "Successful response with benchmark rules list"}
  resp 400 {"$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"}
===== GET /v1/rules
Returns list of rules for specific baseline and their sources
  param {"$ref": "#/components/parameters/X-Environment-Id"}
  param {"description": "Given baseline ID", "in": "query", "name": "baseline-id", "required": true, "schema": {"minLength": 1, "type": "string"}}
  resp 200 {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/SourcedRules"}}}, "description": "Successful operation result"}
  resp 400 {"description": "Missing or empty baseline ID"}

